WEBVTT

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.890
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:31.230
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:39.000
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.100
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.810
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:57.590
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:04.560
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.490
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:20.170
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.890
Ah, time for
lunch!

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.030
What's going on?

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.620
What's going on?
Hi, Nakajima. Forget about having lunch.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.530
Why's that?

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.770
Why's that?
I don't think there's anything left.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:43.900
I don't think there's anything left.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.870
Hmm?

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.810
Hey, that's my tempura rice!

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.880
Really?

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.780
So give it back!
Really?

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.320
FILE. 45
A SUMMER'S
DAY TOGETHER

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.030
What on earth are
they thinking?

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:18.470
Coming here and wolfing down every
single morsel in the cafeteria.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.270
Currently, Toukairin's up 10 to nothing.
Natsumi's in a real slump.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.240
I never would have guessed
that Tsujimoto would lose.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.970
I can't stand it! Every time Toukairin comes
around, all our food disappears!

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:33.950
But I wonder...

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:34.480
Thanks.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.480
...why Toukairin comes to Bokuto Station?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:44.820
Yeah, now that you mention it, we don't
have any rescue classes today, do we?

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:49.700
He drops in a lot, considering
he has no reason to be here.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:54.700
If he's just looking for a place to eat, there
are lots of other cafeterias to choose from.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:59.460
Maybe he likes the food
here better. It is good.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.410
Or maybe there's someone
here he's got a crush on!

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.080
I'm sure that's it!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.320
No way.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:06.880
Wait.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.950
Huh?

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:12.180
That's probably right.
Huh?

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.390
Come off it, Natsumi.
Get over it.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.460
All you did was lose an eating
competition, that's all.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.730
Why can't I beat that
stupid jerk?!

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.800
This is probably good for you. Even
the best have their betters.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.930
Just watch me next time. I'm going to eat
10 pork on rice, and 50 plates of gyoza!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.380
Stop!

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.870
Stop!
What?

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.450
What is it?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.750
What is it?
I'm going to offer a prayer for victory.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.620
Hmm?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:48.620
"Jirikihongan Temple"

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.400
Hello, Oshou!

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.340
Hello, you two!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.110
It's been a long time.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.710
Following the scent of these sweet cakes?

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.250
Can we have some?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.380
Certainly. Help yourselves.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.780
Thanks!

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:17.750
You're eating again?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:18.520
Hello.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.490
Hmm?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.790
Nice to see you.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.390
Oh, I see you know each other.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.860
What are you doing here?

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.630
Uh...

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.330
The Section Chief introduced us. We
sometimes play shogi together.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.740
Yes, this young fellow
is my opponent.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.240
Uh... Coming.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.280
I'll be right
back.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.780
I didn't know that.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.980
Here, kitty-kitty.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.790
Come here,
cat.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:04.020
Last time it was a puppy, and now this cat.
Seems like you're an animal person.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.940
I don't mind them.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:10.310
I don't mind them.
I've been meaning to ask you...

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:10.440
I've been meaning to ask you...

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.770
What's that?
I've been meaning to ask you...

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:15.540
You seem to hang around Bokuto Station
a lot. Do you have work there?

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.110
Sure I do.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.520
Where?

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.790
Here and there

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.020
Hey, little pussycat.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.750
Oh, brother.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.330
What's the matter?

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.380
Well.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:34.760
I have to make an out-of-town delivery next
Sunday, but something has come up.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.890
What am I going
to do?

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:42.130
Why don't you let us
deliver it for you?

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:47.270
We're off-duty on Sunday, and we were
thinking of going for a drive anyway.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.740
It'd be no problem
for us to take it.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.910
Is that so? That would
be a big help.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.690
This is the package, right here.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.460
This is the package, right here.
Who should we take it to?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:58.590
Who should we take it to?

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.110
To my mother, in Ibaraki.
Who should we take it to?

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.730
Your mother? How
old is she?

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:10.630
She's 90 this year. She's so full of beans,
I don't know what to do with her.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:11.600
I appreciate this.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.160
I appreciate this.
No problem! Oh! Sorry!

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.640
Sorry, pussycat. I didn't
mean to step on you.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.220
Wow! What a great day!

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.880
Wow! What a great day!
Yeah, perfect for a drive.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:07.720
Today, I'm going to leave my
troubles completely behind!

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:12.160
Are you still thinking about
losing to Toukairin?

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.530
Not necessarily.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.400
Not necessarily.
Excuse me. I just think you're a good pair.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:22.530
Toukairin's just about the only person who
can match your own strength, Natsumi.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:28.140
Give it a rest. I like distinguished men.
Anyway, he's younger than me.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.370
So what do you think
of Toukairin?

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.720
Nothing, I just hate him winning all the time.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.390
You sure do hate losing, don't you?

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.380
And you don't?!

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.330
Shall we get going?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.190
Okay!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.260
Huh?

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.570
Lieutenant Toukairin.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.540
Hey, what's that?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.780
Hey, what's that?
You got it.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.800
Then what about that one?
You got it.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.810
Oshou accidentally gave
you the wrong box.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.250
No way!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.720
Don't, Natsumi.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:12.960
There's nothing on it.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.690
Oh.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:18.490
Boy, he's always in such
a rush, that's why.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.790
So why did he give
that to you?

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.600
I happened to have a day off, too.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.860
But riding that bike all the way to Ibaraki?

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.540
I come here a lot, actually.
I'm used to it.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.510
Used to it?!

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:34.240
I knew we were taking our time, but boy...

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.210
Well, shall we?

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.040
You mean?

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:42.170
Oshou's mother lives in that
village, right down there.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:06.870
"lnari Shrine"

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.810
Wow! Look at the size of this
thatch-roofed house!

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:33.070
Hello!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:37.570
Is anybody
home?

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:41.870
Hello.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:46.110
It's not that son
of mine, is it?

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:52.050
You must be Oshou's mother. We're
here to deliver the scroll.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:56.960
That we are!

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:00.090
My goodness, that
son of mine.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.530
Asking you to come all the
way out here, in his place.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.140
Not a problem. We're the ones who offered.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.130
That's right. Think nothing of it.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:13.470
Still, it's a terribly long
way for you to come.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.350
I know. Why don't you stay for lunch?

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.820
Gee, I don't know.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:23.250
Nothing fancy. Don't be strangers.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:26.480
I understand, it's just that
these two have...

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:29.990
Thanks for inviting us! In fact, we didn't
really have a big enough lunch anyway!

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.000
Thank you, we'd like to stay.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.730
Good, I'm glad to hear it.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:41.340
You two can't go cleaning
out her entire kitchen.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.570
Go and buy enough food for yourselves.

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.870
Okay.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.480
I'll stay here and help her prepare.
Come back soon.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.250
We will.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.280
I hope those two
will be all right.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:25.210
Hurry up and get
back here!

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:29.320
Um...

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:31.220
Hmm?

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:34.990
Oh, uh...

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.590
It's beautiful.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:37.820
Hmm?

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:41.260
It is. Look at these
sunflowers!

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.090
Wow!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:49.070
You're from Toyama Prefecture, aren't
you? It must be beautiful.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:53.040
There's nothing but mountains,
but I like it.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:57.040
Is that how you got into Mountain
Search and Rescue?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.950
Sergeant Tsujimoto. There's some place
I'd like to take you. Do you mind?

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.690
Uh, no.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.720
"Liquor"

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.950
Thank you very
much.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:36.280
Wow!

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:49.520
How 'bout we go
down there?

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:10.320
"Ikenaga"

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:13.710
Does this grave belong to
someone you know?

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:21.060
He liked sake and he liked the ocean.
He loved the mountains.

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:57.160
<i>"Toukairin! You've got</i>
<i>to keep going."</i>

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.670
<i>"You go on, Mr.</i>
<i>Ikenaga."</i>

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.640
<i>"Don't worry</i>
<i>about me."</i>

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:08.270
<i>"Don't be stupid! You save lives. How</i>
<i>can you think of wasting your own!"</i>

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.390
<i>"I see. That's good</i>
<i>to hear."</i>

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:22.750
<i>"Yes, we're fine.</i>
<i>Roger..."</i>

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.090
<i>"So, the rescue was</i>
<i>successful."</i>

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.060
<i>"Really. That's</i>
<i>great."</i>

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:31.530
<i>"And we'll descend after dawn."</i>

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.560
<i>"And we'll descend after dawn."</i>
<i>"Yes."</i>

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.700
<i>"Eat up."</i>

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:45.570
<i>"Nothing ever spoils your appetite,</i>
<i>does it? That's a good thing."</i>

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:52.210
<i>"Strange, isn't it?"</i>

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:58.590
<i>"That a snowstorm would remind me</i>
<i>of the ocean in the summertime."</i>

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:01.890
<i>"When I was a child, I would</i>
<i>play there all day long."</i>

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:06.900
<i>"So you like the ocean, as</i>
<i>well as the mountains."</i>

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.630
<i>"I like both. They're</i>
<i>both so huge."</i>

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.130
<i>"I prefer the</i>
<i>mountains."</i>

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.180
<i>"I see. You must come and stay</i>
<i>at my house sometime."</i>

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:22.380
<i>"When you see the blue of the ocean,</i>
<i>you'll want to swim forever."</i>

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:25.280
<i>"I'm really not a very</i>
<i>good swimmer."</i>

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:29.780
<i>"Then we'll make</i>
<i>you better."</i>

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:41.230
So what happened?

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:47.240
He got sick. He used to be so
strong. Stronger than most.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:55.780
What a beautiful ocean. Makes
you want to swim forever.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:07.900
We should go. Kobayakawa is waiting.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.870
Uh... Yeah.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:29.150
I appreciate your lending a hand.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.150
No problem. I like cooking.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.960
You seem very organized.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.190
Not at all.

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:38.390
You must have someone to cook for.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.530
Huh?

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:46.460
At my age, you can tell things like that.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.270
He's a very
lucky man.

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:56.900
<i>"Kobayakawa..."</i>

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.810
Those two sure are
taking a long time.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.660
Okay, are you ready?

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.320
Ready.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.730
Here goes!

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:16.060
My, oh my.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:20.000
I sure do appreciate
this.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.530
Look at all the stuff
he gave us.

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:31.840
It all looks so good. Let's hurry and
give it to Oshou's Mom to cook up.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.180
Yeah.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:37.250
I think we'd better run, though.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:41.160
I think we'd better run, though.
Hmm?

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:02.970
Look at this
rain.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:09.240
It's just a shower.
It'll stop soon.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:15.620
Look at it coming
down!

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.650
Unreal!

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.600
Um...

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.700
You're getting soaked.
You can come closer.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:46.880
Why did you take
me there...

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:52.190
...to that place that's
so special to you?

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.770
Here, have one.

00:18:55.770 --> 00:18:59.760
Here, have one.
Thanks.

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:04.870
You have to eat when you can. Otherwise,
you won't have energy when you need it.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.340
Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:11.710
Mm, it's good. Nothing like veggies
straight off the farm.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:13.620
We're back.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.290
We're back.
Natsumi! What took you so long?!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:16.420
Natsumi! What took you so long?!

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:17.490
Sorry.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:21.220
I thought you'd never get back.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.730
We were worried about you.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:24.920
How come?

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.800
I thought you might have had a fight.

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.390
Of course we didn't.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:35.440
We brought this.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.230
We brought this.
Here! Your hair!

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:38.600
Bring it over.

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:39.640
Okay.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.370
Aah!

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:44.450
Ooh! That feels
better.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:57.630
More rice!

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:58.860
Me, too!

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:00.520
Him, too!

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.220
Coming up.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:13.800
Watching them reminds me of my husband
and I, when we were young.

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:16.450
What's that?

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:18.280
They're a lovely couple.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:21.270
No, they're nothing like that at all.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:25.580
Is that a fact? I could have sworn
that they were in love.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:27.590
It couldn't be...

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:31.580
At my age, you know about these things.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.870
Thanks for lunch, Mrs. Oshou.

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.600
Good-bye.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:46.680
Come again!

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:49.610
We will!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.660
I hope he's all right riding
back on his bike.

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:11.900
He said he'd
be fine.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:14.170
Yeah, but still.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:17.470
What is it?

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:19.780
You sure seem concerned.

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:22.210
I do? It's just, uh...

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:27.010
He's not as bad as I thought, after
all. Anyway, just forget it.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.200
No way!

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:43.790
I don't believe him.

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:49.500
Hmm. I sure don't under-
stand that guy.

00:21:55.740 --> 00:22:01.950
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:09.260
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:18.760
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:28.610
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:32.610 --> 00:22:42.850
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:51.070
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:59.710
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.940 --> 00:23:07.780
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:17.360
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:24.800
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.100
"Golden Opportunity"

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:32.270
Yoriko, how is your ventriliquism practice
for traffic safety class going?

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:35.770
No problem. You can
count on me.

00:23:36.710 --> 00:23:37.870
Is that so...

00:23:38.050 --> 00:23:38.780
Cut it out, Natsumi!

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.510
Oh. Sorry! Sorry!

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:42.580
Hey that's Toukairin, the Lieutenant!

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:46.650
Next time on You're Under
Arrest, File 46...

00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:48.760
...Toukairin's Challenge.

00:23:48.890 --> 00:23:51.890
Is that a kendo duel?
